    "font" : "NewCenturySchlbk-Bold",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "‘‘§3318. Lactation room in public buildings"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 39,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 202.0, 394.667, 363.333, 405.333 ],
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "((a) DEFINITIONS. In this section:"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 40,
    "level" : "1",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 201.0, 351.667, 503.0, 396.0 ],
    "font" : "NewCenturySchlbk-Roman",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : ".—The term ‘appropriate authority’ means the head of a Federal agency, the Architect of the Capitol, or other official authority responsible for the operation of a public building. ‘‘(2) C OVERED PUBLIC BUILDING .—The term ‘covered public"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 41,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 201.667, 312.333, 503.333, 356.667 ],
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "<(2) COVERED PUBLIC BUILDING.~The term 'covered public building means a public building (as defined in section 3301) that is open to the   public and contains a and includes a building listed in section 6301 or 5101"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 42,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 202.333, 292.333, 502.0, 316.0 ],
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "((3) LACTATION ROOM. The term lactation room' means a hygienic place; other than a bathroom; that"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 43,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 249.667, 284.333, 365.0, 296.333 ],
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "Á) is shielded from view;"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 44,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 245.667, 273.0, 386.333, 286.333 ],
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "'(B) is free from intrusion; and"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 45,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 221.0, 244.667, 502.333, 278.0 ],
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "<(C contains a chair, a working surface; and, if the public building is otherwise suppliea  with electricity, an electrical outlet."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 46,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 181.333, 194.667, 503.333, 246.667 ],
    "font" : "NewCenturySchlbk-Roman",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "‘‘(b) section (c), the appropriate authority of a covered public building shall ensure that the building contains a lactation room that is made available for use by members of the public to express breast milk. ‘‘(c) E XCEPTIONS .—A covered public building may be excluded"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 47,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 181.333, 162.0, 502.667, 198.0 ],
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "EXCEPTIONS.A covered public building may be excluded from the requirement in subsection (b) at the discretion of the appropriate authority if \"(c)"
  }, {
